is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: leaf_router_0_0
diagnosis_text:
Affected component: FRRouting (bgpd) on leaf_router_0_0. Mechanism: With bgpd down, leaf_router_0_0 neither advertises its local subnet (10.0.0.0/24) nor learns the remote subnet (10.0.1.0/24). As a result, both edge hosts receive ICMP “Destination Net Unreachable” from their local leaf gateways.

Evidence:
- From pc_0_0 to pc_0_1: “From 10.0.0.1 Destination Net Unreachable.” From pc_0_1 to pc_0_0: “From 10.0.1.1 Destination Net Unreachable.” This indicates route absence on the leaves.
- leaf_router_0_0 has no learned routes (only connected: 10.0.0.0/24, 172.16.0.4/31, 172.16.0.8/31) and “bgpd is not running”; systemd shows “frr.service … Active: inactive (dead).”
- Both spines show their sessions to AS 6520
