[FINAL-TEXT] === DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: leaf_router_0_0
diagnosis_text:
Affected component: FRRouting (bgpd) on leaf_router_0_0. Mechanism: With bgpd down, leaf_router_0_0 neither advertises its local subnet (10.0.0.0/24) nor learns the remote subnet (10.0.1.0/24). As a result, both edge hosts receive ICMP “Destination Net Unreachable” from their local leaf gateways.

Evidence:
- From pc_0_0 to pc_0_1: “From 10.0.0.1 Destination Net Unreachable.” From pc_0_1 to pc_0_0: “From 10.0.1.1 Destination Net Unreachable.” This indicates route absence on the leaves.
- leaf_router_0_0 has no learned routes (only connected: 10.0.0.0/24, 172.16.0.4/31, 172.16.0.8/31) and “bgpd is not running”; systemd shows “frr.service … Active: inactive (dead).”
- Both spines show their sessions to AS 65200 (leaf_router_0_0) stuck in “Active” (spine_router_0_0 neighbor 172.16.0.5; spine_router_0_1 neighbor 172.16.0.9), while they successfully learn 10.0.1.0/24 from leaf_router_0_1. leaf_router_0_1 BGP “PfxRcd 0” further confirms nothing is learned from the fabric because 10.0.0.0/24 is missing.

Localization: leaf_router_0_0 control plane (FRR/bgpd), affecting its uplinks (eth0/eth1) and default gateway function for pc_0_0 (eth2).

Root cause: FRR service is stopped on leaf_router_0_0, leaving no BGP sessions to the spines.

Corrective fix: Restart FRR on leaf_router_0_0 (ensure bgpd starts and is enabled at boot), verify BGP neighbors to both spines establish and that 10.0.1.0/24 appears in leaf_router_0_0’s RIB, and confirm spines learn 10.0.0.0/24. No restart is needed on spine_router_0_0. === END ===